        "text": "DeepSeek is a text output family that also accepts image and text input, and all 14 listed versions publish open weights, so self hosting and inspection are possible across the line. Context windows run from 64000 to 1048576 tokens, and 12 of the 14 versions support reasoning. The spread of versions matters when choosing: the newest entries carry the largest windows and outputs, while older ones are smaller. Price varies widely, with input from $0.02 to $0.7 per million tokens and output from $0.06 to $4.2, so long outputs on the pricier tiers are the main cost risk. The facts suggest the family suits long context work, reasoning tasks and image plus text input, with cheap high volume options available. Limits are the text only output, the older small windows, and the higher output prices on some tiers.",
